• New bug, found by running the binary: when yoyo can't write its output (full disk, tested by sending output to /dev/full):
  • plain text and stream-json output exit 0 with no message, so a script thinks it succeeded and the reply is lost;
  • --output-format json crashes ("failed printing to stdout: No space left on device", exit 101);
  • -o /dev/full already handles it correctly (error message, exit 1).

  Claude Code fixed this same bug for claude -p in 2.1.330 (Nov 20). There's no existing issue and I haven't filed one. The fix has to keep yoyo | head ending quietly when the reader goes away, as cat does. I didn't find where text mode swallows the error.
